@page "/docs/primitives/installation"

<DocsPage Title="Installation" Description="Add Blazix.Primitives to your Blazor app and set it up.">
    <DocsHeading Title="Install the library" />
    <p>Add the package to your Blazor app:</p>
    <CodeFigure Code="dotnet add package Blazix.Primitives" Language="bash" />
    <p>
        All the primitives are in this one package. You don't add a <code>&lt;script&gt;</code> tag: each primitive's
        JavaScript module ships inside the package and is imported the first time the primitive is used. If you use the
        styled components, <code>dnx Blazix.Cli init</code> has already added it.
    </p>

    <DocsHeading Title="Set up" />
    <DocsHeading Level="3" Title="Render mode" />
    <p>The primitives need an interactive render mode. They're tested with Interactive Server, for example set for the whole app:</p>
    <CodeFigure Code="@RenderModeCode" Title="Components/App.razor" />
    <DocsHeading Level="3" Title="Imports" />
    <p>Import the namespace in the files that use the primitives, or once in <code>_Imports.razor</code>:</p>
    <CodeFigure Code="@ImportsCode" Title="Components/_Imports.razor" />
    <p>
        Some parts share a name with a styled component (<code>AccordionItem</code>, <code>DialogTrigger</code>...), and
        Razor can't tell two components with the same tag apart. If you use both, import <code>Blazix.Primitives</code> only in
        the folders that use the primitives directly, or write the full name, as in
        <code>&lt;Blazix.Primitives.DialogPopup&gt;</code>.
    </p>
    <DocsHeading Level="3" Title="Popups" />
    <p>
        Popups such as Dialog, Menu and Popover render in the browser's top layer, so they appear above the rest of the page
        whatever its <code>z-index</code> and <code>overflow</code> styles. They aren't moved into a portal: they stay where
        you wrote them in the DOM, so cascading values, CSS isolation and a <code>.dark</code> class on any wrapper still
        apply to them.
    </p>

    <DocsHeading Title="Next steps" />
    <p>
        <a href="/docs/primitives">Assemble your first component</a>, then read the handbook on
        <a href="/docs/primitives/styling">styling</a> the primitives.
    </p>
</DocsPage>


@code {
    private const string RenderModeCode = """
        <Routes @rendermode="InteractiveServer" />
        """;

    private const string ImportsCode = """
        @using Blazix.Primitives
        """;
}
